<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-14497] Move background task deletion at the end of next checkpoint</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-14497</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;In &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; has been described scenario of the race that makes possible a situation when information from metastore has been deleted and part of the index is still present in the storage.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Actually, fix in &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; that has been done in slightly different way, however, it strongly decreases possibility of the race. Removal of the background task has been moved to beginning of the next checkpoint. It was done this way, because the problem was in case when node unexpectedly failed in the middle of next checkpoint and after restart task failed on check of deleted index metaPage. The check was done in &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In current issue, we only move background task deletion at the end of the next checkpoint.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13382&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;IGNITE-13382&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
 &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-14447&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;IGNITE-14447&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
